<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ecuadorian War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1820">1820</a>–<a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-wars-of-independence">Spanish American wars of independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ecuadorian War of Independence was fought between 1820 and 1822 to free the Royal Audience of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> from Spanish rule. It began with the revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> in October 1820 and ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-jose-de-sucre">Antonio José de Sucre</a> defeated the royalists at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pichincha">Battle of Pichincha</a> above Quito on 24 May 1822. The territory then joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ecuadorian-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Ecuadorian War of Independence" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Varios autores · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collage_de_la_Indepedencia_de_Ecuador.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
